<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Glyph rasterisation, and nothing else (D84).

    **The only project in this tree allowed to know what a font file is.** It implements
    `IGlyphRasteriser`, which is declared in Content, and nothing references it except the
    composition root in Viewer3D. So the interface lives in the low, stable, portable project and
    the implementation in the high, volatile, platform-bound one - which is the direction dependency
    inversion asks for.

    **It is its own project rather than part of Viewer3D on the owner's direction**: "it might not
    becuase of MVP, it might need its own project", and then the reason - "we want the compile time
    safety from MVP". Viewer3D is the View; a rasteriser is infrastructure that happens to need a
    Windows API, the same category as Render and Logging, both of which were split out for exactly
    this reason. A layering rule in a document is a rule someone breaks by accident; a layering rule
    expressed as a project reference is one the compiler refuses.

    **net10.0-windows, and that is the whole reason the project exists.** System.Drawing.Common is
    Windows-only by design since .NET 7. Putting it in Render would have undone D60/D61 and thrown
    away the reason PngWriter was hand-written; putting it in Content would have broken the Linux
    measurement boxes, and broken them as a build failure that Stryker scores as a SURVIVING MUTANT
    rather than reporting as an error.

    **What is here is an approximation until vguimatsurface is decompiled**, and it says so at the
    call sites rather than claiming parity it has not earned. In VGUI an outline is not a font
    feature - it is Valve's own post-process over the GDI bitmap, along with blur, dropshadow and
    scanlines - and that code is not in source-sdk-2013.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0-windows</TargetFramework>
    <RootNamespace>Tf2DemoSalvage.Fonts</RootNamespace>
    <UseWindowsForms>false</UseWindowsForms>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Tf2DemoSalvage.Fonts.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="System.Drawing.Common" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Tf2DemoSalvage.Content\Tf2DemoSalvage.Content.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
